// expect-error: function pointer requires an initializer
// BUG-856, the site that had drifted: the non-null-funcptr rule existed only in
// the LOCAL var-decl copy of the check. Its GLOBAL sibling checked `*T` data
// pointers and never grew the funcptr arm, so this global auto-zeroed to NULL
// and `gop(1, 2)` emitted a raw call through address 0.
//
// Both sites now run the same query (nonnull_zero_hole), so they cannot drift
// apart again.
*(u32, u32) -> u32 gop;

u32 main() {
    return gop(1, 2);
}
